    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s action, **Cal Raleigh** (78.02) and **Bryce Harper** (76.79) headline our lineup as the premier starts. **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against J. Lopez, where his power profile aligns perfectly with the favorable park factors and the pitcher\u2019s inflated 4.77 xERA. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** finds himself in an enviable position against G. Holmes; his elite xwOBA metrics combined with a solid #3 order placement make him a near-lock for production. **Lawrence Butler** (67.93) also deserves attention; despite the tough matchup against B. Miller, his massive 13% boost from dynamic platoon modeling and favorable park factors make him a high-upside play for our outfield.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dylan Beavers** (49.94), who narrowly missed the cut. While he possesses an ideal #1 order spot, his efficiency score was severely hampered by the matchup against Cease, whose 3.02 xERA significantly suppresses our offensive expectations. We opted to lean into the higher-scoring profiles of **Justin Crawford** (62.22) and **Jonathan Aranda** (62.41), both of whom are facing pitchers with significantly higher xERA profiles than Cease. We continue to monitor **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.39) on the bench; while he carries favorable wind conditions, the \"Lineup Pending\" status and the presence of a tough arm like Nick Pivetta kept him out of the active roster to preserve our game caps.\n\nWe are navigating the board with a focus on maximizing SB opportunities, which keeps **Justin Crawford** and **Luis Arraez** in the mix despite some variance in their daily projections. We remain concerned about the lower-end of our infield rotation, specifically **Masyn Winn** and **Alex Freeland**, who both carry scores below 50 due to their #9 order slots. We will be closely watching the weather and any late-breaking lineup changes for **Jung Hoo Lee**, but for now, the path forward is clear: ride the power of **Cal Raleigh** and **Bryce Harper** and look for efficiency from the bottom-third of the order against weaker arms.",
